```mermaid
graph TB
    Cost[Original Cost J<br/>= 1/m Σ L ŷ, y] --> Choice{Add<br/>Regularization?}
    
    Choice -->|L2 default| L2[J + λ/2m × ‖W‖²]
    Choice -->|L1 sparsity| L1[J + λ/2m × ‖W‖₁]
    Choice -->|No| Plain[Original cost only<br/>May overfit]
    
    L2 --> L2Effect[Weights stay small<br/>but rarely zero<br/>= weight decay]
    L1 --> L1Effect[Many weights = 0<br/>= sparse model<br/>= feature selection]
    
    L2Effect --> Update2[Update: W = W·1-αλ/m - α·dW<br/>W shrinks each step]
    L1Effect --> Update1[Update has subgradient<br/>pushes weights to 0]
    
    style L2 fill:#c8e6c9
    style L1 fill:#fff9c4
    style L2Effect fill:#a5d6a7
    style L1Effect fill:#fff59d
```

## Effect of λ (Lambda)

```
λ value      | Effect              | Result
-------------|---------------------|----------
λ = 0        | No regularization   | Original loss (overfits)
λ = 0.001    | Very mild           | Slight smoothing
λ = 0.01     | Mild (default)      | Good for most cases
λ = 0.1      | Moderate            | Stronger regularization
λ = 1.0      | Strong              | Significant weight decay
λ = 100      | Too strong          | Underfits (bias too high)
```
